<td id="S4.T2.3.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.3.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.5729</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.3.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" rowspan="5"><span id="S4.T2.3.7.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=1.20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=1.20</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.3.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T2.3.7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Plug-in</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.3.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_rr ltx_border_t">Split</th>
<td id="S4.T2.3.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1.3221</td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1.4004</td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.7.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.2722</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.3.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_rr">Split + Synthetic</th>
<td id="S4.T2.3.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.3371</td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.4385</td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.2810</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.3.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" rowspan="3"><span id="S4.T2.3.9.1.1" class="ltx_text">RL</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.3.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_rr ltx_border_t">Split</th>
<td id="S4.T2.3.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1.1745</td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.9.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.1120</td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.9.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.5215</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.3.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_rr">Bootstrap</th>
<td id="S4.T2.3.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.1768</td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.1061</td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.5427</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.3.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_rr">Split + Synthetic</th>
<td id="S4.T2.3.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">1.1704</td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.0892</td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.11.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T2.3.11.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.5707</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance of different portfolio strategies with and without synthetic paths.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The results are summarized in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4 Empirical Study ‣ Data-driven generative simulation of SDEs using diffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, which suggest that including synthetic paths fails to improve the plug-in policy. On the other hand, introducing synthetic paths to the market simulator provides a significant performance boost to the original RL policy which already decisively outperforms the plug-in policy. Indeed, when the synthetic paths are added, the RL agent achieves the highest Sharpe ratios, primarily due to reductions of the variance of the terminal wealth. Intuitively, the synthetic paths enable the RL agent to explore more possible market scenarios and learn a more robust policy.</p>
</div>
</section>
